@@ portable
(** Bounded, advisory observations of an XMP packet.  This module performs no
    file I/O and makes no claim about RDF value equivalence, rendered pixels, or
    which metadata is safe to merge. *)

type category = Descriptive | Rendering | Identity | Workflow | Opaque

type property = {
  name : string;
  (** Expanded name in Clark notation [{namespace-URI}local-name]. *)
  category : category;
  digest : string;
  (** Raw 32-byte SHA-256 of the versioned encoding/context transcript described
      below.  This is independent of Unison's archive fingerprint. *)
}

type observation = { properties : property list }

val observe : string -> (observation, string) result
(** Accepts at most 1 MiB of UTF-8 XML 1.0, with optional UTF-8 BOM, XML declaration,
    packet processing instructions, and an [adobe:ns:meta/] [xmpmeta] envelope.
    The RDF root contains either one anonymous Description, or descriptions
    carrying the same explicit [rdf:about] subject (including an explicit empty
    subject).  An absent subject is never equated with an explicit empty subject.
    Description attributes
    and direct child properties are observed in packet order; duplicate expanded
    property names are rejected even if their bytes agree.

    Attribute encodings are the exact bytes between their quotation marks.
    Child encodings are the entire exact element span, including opening/closing
    markup, descendants, comments, CDATA, and nested masks or AI data.  A digest
    additionally binds every sorted in-scope prefix/decoded-URI mapping, including
    declarations on the property element.  Ancestor rebinding therefore changes
    the digest; an unused binding change can conservatively do so as well.

    Transcript: ASCII [Unison-XMP-observation], NUL, ASCII [v1], NUL; one byte
    [A] for an attribute value or [E] for a child element; a big-endian unsigned
    32-bit binding count; for each binding sorted by prefix, length-prefixed
    prefix then URI; finally length-prefixed exact encoding bytes.  Each length
    is a big-endian unsigned 32-bit byte count.  No XML/RDF canonicalization,
    entity-value normalization, or alias equivalence is asserted by the digest.

    Limits: 128 properties, 512 bytes per expanded name or namespace URI,
    128 bytes per prefix, 256 bytes per local name, 64 active namespace bindings
    (including the predefined [xml] binding), depth 64, 8192 content/element
    nodes, 256 attributes per element, and 16384 attributes in the packet.
    XML QNames are restricted to ASCII.  Namespace URI whitespace, controls,
    unsupported ASCII URI characters (including braces), and malformed percent
    escapes are rejected, so expanded names are unambiguous.  Predefined and numeric
    character references are accepted and validated; namespace values decode
    them for namespace resolution.  DTDs, external/general entities, UTF-16,
    XML 1.1, nested processing instructions, [rdf:ID]/[rdf:nodeID] subjects,
    XML-namespace attributes on structural Description elements (including
    [xml:base], [xml:id], [xml:lang], and [xml:space]), and unsupported envelope/RDF
    structures return a bounded [Error] reason without an input excerpt.

    [rdf:about], namespace declarations, the XML/packet declarations, and
    [xmpmeta] toolkit attributes are structural and are not emitted as
    properties.  This observation is consequently neither a complete packet
    fingerprint nor an Adobe rendering/dependency interpretation. *)
